{"authored" [{"question" "q-95084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y},x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s)+(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s})\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2-2\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s} \\\\  & =-2-2{cot}^{2}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8194713c58a546b3a89b58adc8494cb9415333032cb9763dd1edd221da5805b" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{sec}^{2}⁡2s"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cot}⁡2s"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s+{csc}^{2}⁡2s"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+y}$ and $y={e}^{-x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}+\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8194713c58a546b3a89b58adc8494cb9415333032cb9763dd1edd221da5805b" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} 