per/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x+1}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{y}{(x+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{x+1}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{x+1}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}(x+1)-{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8194713c58a546b3a89b58adc8494cb9415333032cb9763dd1edd221da5805b" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.t