selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}{(x+1)^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-95122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-1)}{(x+1)^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ where $x=t+s$ and $y=ts.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =ts{e}^{t+s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{t+s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(ts{e}^{t+s})(1)+({e}^{t+s})(t) \\\\  & =t{e}^{t+s}(s+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8194713c58a546b3a89b58adc8494cb9415333032cb9763dd1edd221da5805b" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "s{e}^{t+s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "s{e}^{t+s}(t+1)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t{e}^{t+s}(s+1)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t{e}^{t+s}(s-t)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-170673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{t+s}(s+t)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f(x,y)=2x+xy,$ where $x=s{e}^{s}$ and $y=t{e}^{s}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2+t{e}^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =s{e}^{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =0, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & ={e}^{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(2+t{e}^{s})(0)+(s{e}^{s})({e}^{s}) \\\\  & =s{e}^{2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8194713c58a546b3a89b58adc8494cb9415333032cb9763dd1edd221da5805b" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-2y,$ where $x=s{t}^{2}$ and $y={s}^{3}-t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/assets/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =({s}^{3}-t)^{2}={s}^{6}-2{s}^{3}t+{t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2(s{t}^{2})({s}^{3}-t)-2=2{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-2s{t}^{3}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & ={t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =({s}^{6}-2{s}^{3}t+{t}^{2})({t}^{2})+(2{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-2s{t}^{3}-2)(3{s}^{2}) \\\\  & ={s}^{6}{t}^{2}-2{s}^{3}{t}^{3}+{t}^{4}+6{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-6{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6{s}^{2} \\\\  & =7{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-8{s}^{3}{t}^{3}-6{s}^{2}+{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8194713c58a546b3a89b58adc8494cb9415333032cb9763dd1edd221da5805b" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_sha256" "dab043a8fe9b126d8ee518c87a90350ca99ee102333d2a371161375be74ff4b7" "basis" 1656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{s}^{6}{t}^{2}-6{s}^{2}+{t}^{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044606/state.json" "file_